==Russian==
{{wikipedia|lang=ru}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ru|ǵʰelh₃}}
From {{inh|ru|sla-pro|*zolto}} (Old Church Slavonic {{m|cu|злато|tr=zlato}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|ru}} {{m|ine-pro|*ǵʰelh₃-||yellow; gleam; to shine}}, probably through a later form {{m|ine-pro||*ǵʰl̥h₃-tó-m|gold}}. Cognate with Ukrainian {{m|uk|золото|tr=zoloto}}, Belarusian {{m|be|золата|tr=zolata}}, Bulgarian {{m|bg|злато|tr=zlato}}, Serbian {{m|sh|злато|tr=zlato|sc=Cyrl}}, Slovene {{m|sl|zlato}}, Czech {{m|cs|zlato}}, Slovak {{m|sk|zlato}}, Polish {{m|pl|złoto}}. The Indo-European root is also the source of Latvian {{m|lv|zelts}} and Proto-Germanic {{m|gem-pro|*gulþą}} (whence English {{m|en|gold}}).

